1
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:08,400
In the winter of 1634, an extraordinary man began a perilous
journey into the North American wilderness.

2
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:10,800
Black Robe is a adventure, drama, history film directed by Bruce Beresford.

3
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:13,200
Missionary Father LaForgue travels to the New World in hopes of
converting Algonquin Indians to Catholicism.

4
00:16:09,600 --> 00:16:15,600
Accepted, though warily, by the Indians, LaForgue travels with the Indians using
his strict Catholic rules and ideals to try and impose his religion.

5
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:18,000
Laforgue, played by Lothaire Bluteau.

6
00:24:14,400 --> 00:24:20,400
Annuka, played by Sandrine Holt.

7
00:28:16,799 --> 00:28:22,799
Chomina, played by August Schellenberg.

8
00:32:19,200 --> 00:32:25,200
Chomina's Wife, played by Tantoo Cardinal.

9
00:36:21,599 --> 00:36:27,599
Neehatin, played by Lawrence Bayne.

10
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:30,000
Daniel, played by Aden Young.

11
00:44:26,400 --> 00:44:32,400
Black Robe is a 1991 historical drama film directed by Bruce Beresford,
adapted by Brian Moore from his 1985 novel of the same name.

12
00:48:28,800 --> 00:48:34,800
Set in the 17th century, it depicts the adventures of a Jesuit
missionary tasked with founding a mission in New France.

13
00:52:31,200 --> 00:52:37,200
To do so, he must traverse 2,400 km of harsh wilderness with the help of a group of
Algonquins, facing danger from both the unfamiliar environment and rival tribes.

14
00:56:33,599 --> 00:56:39,599
The title refers to the nickname given to the Jesuits by the
Algonquins, referring to his black cassock.

15
01:00:36,000 --> 01:00:42,000
The film stars Lothaire Bluteau in the title role, with other cast members: Aden Young, Sandrine
Holt, Tantoo Cardinal, August Schellenberg, Gordon Tootoosis and Raoul Trujillo.

16
01:04:38,400 --> 01:04:44,400
It was the first official co-production between a
Canadian film team and an Australian one.

17
01:08:40,800 --> 01:08:46,800
It was shot mostly in the Canadian province of Quebec.

18
01:12:43,199 --> 01:12:49,199
It was Young and Holt's film debut.

19
01:16:45,600 --> 01:16:51,600
Black Robe premiered at the 1991 Toronto International Film Festival and was given a wide
release on 6 October, becoming the highest-grossing Canadian film of 1991.

20
01:20:48,000 --> 01:20:54,000
It received generally positive reviews and won several accolades.

21
01:24:50,400 --> 01:24:56,400
It was nominated for ten Genie Awards and won six, including Best Motion Picture, Best Director
(Beresford), Best Adapted Screenplay (Moore) and Best Supporting Actor (Schellenberg).

22
01:28:52,800 --> 01:28:58,800
It was also nominated for ten AACTA Awards, with
Peter James winning Best Cinematography.

23
01:32:55,199 --> 01:33:01,199
The film explores themes of quebec, wilderness, native
american, journey, jesuits (society of jesus).

24
01:36:57,600 --> 01:37:03,600
The tone is emotional.
